{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G8.DATA_H.DATA_PRESENTATION_AND_IN",
 "title": "Data Presentation and Interpretation",
 "status": "draft: written 18 Nov 2026 offline for Grade 8; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to g are tested; h (use IT) and i (promote use) are not questions. Data is discrete (shoe sizes, scores, sales). Drawing bar and line graphs (a, c) is done on paper; a phone question tests the scale, the bar heights and the choice of graph. The families' old letter b (interpret graphs) covered both bar and line graphs and their old e covered all three averages; each is refiled under KICD's own letter (bar b, line d, mode e, mean f, median g). A skill for comparing the three averages and choosing one carries e, f and g. Finding a missing value from the mean and the new mean after adding a value are filed as mean problems. Teacher to confirm: whether choosing the best average (one family) is taught in Grade 8.",
 "skills": [
  {
